# replay-clip (#550): 10 s of a recorded VR session - a walk-and-turn clip of replay-record.xrs (4500-14500 ms on its
# clock), cut by scripts/dev/clip-to-xrs.ps1 - replayed on the simulated headset as a script: the recorded head, hands,
# fingers and raw inputs go through the simulator's OpenXR poses and actions, and the game answers them as it did.
# The clip's save was the record start's (save9000); the mvp-new-game scenario it was recorded from takes its place.
# The one CI sequence of the feature (coordinator Tests and CI rule 11); the record-and-replay check itself is
# scripts/dev/replay-check.ps1 (hand-run).
@sim replay-clip
@save mvp-new-game
@args --loadslot 0 --seed 4242

@until state eq GAMEPLAY 60s
# (this session is recorded too - every VR session records - but its "[replay] recording" line comes at the first
# playable frame, before this sequence's first mark: replay-check.ps1 reads it from the whole log)
setplayercontrols on
@assert player.controlsBlocked eq false

# The clip's inputs, as the game saw them: a jump from the right stick at 6.7 s, a left grip press at 9.7 s
@log \[vr\] input: jump \(right\.stick_up\) 20s
@log \[vr\] input: left grip down at 10s
@log \[vr\] input: left grip up at 5s
@until vr.sim.pending eq 0 40s
@assert vr.sim.timelineFrame ge 850
@assert errors eq 0
